WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.668
- Welcome to The Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.909
Give it up for my band, y'all,

00:00:02.909 --> 00:00:05.091
playing "Bad Habits" by Ed Sheeran.

00:00:05.091 --> 00:00:06.269
(audience cheering)

00:00:06.269 --> 00:00:07.279
- Yeah!

00:00:07.279 --> 00:00:08.187
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.187 --> 00:00:10.620
So we have someone on the line

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.840
who is very familiar with that song.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.068
Can we say hi to him, everybody?

00:00:15.068 --> 00:00:16.143
What's up, Ed Sheeran?

00:00:17.115 --> 00:00:20.115
(audience cheering)

00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:25.099
- Get it out.

00:00:25.099 --> 00:00:26.320
Get it out, people.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.160
They love you.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.909
It is great to see you again.

00:00:29.909 --> 00:00:31.440
I'm gonna lead with this.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.620
It is absolutely terrifying
to be singing someone's song

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.990
and them listening while you're doing it.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.730
I was like, "Oh my God."

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:39.630
I was like, "It's terrifying."

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.957
I love that song though.

00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:42.180
"Bad Habits" is such a gem.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.013
I love it.

00:00:43.013 --> 00:00:44.139
Why did you write that?

00:00:44.139 --> 00:00:44.972
- Thank you.

00:00:44.972 --> 00:00:46.109
I loved your version by the way.

00:00:46.109 --> 00:00:48.180
I was listening to your version,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.770
wondering whether I
should have actually used

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.000
more electric guitar in it

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.370
'cause it sounded pretty great.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.430
I wrote it

00:00:55.919 --> 00:00:57.630
quite by accident?

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.800
I was working with

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.470
the two people that I made the
album with, Johnny and Fred,

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.410
and Fred is primarily
like a dance producer

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:10.410
and he played me a tune that
he was just about to release

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.270
that was a really,
really heavy dance tune.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:13.147
And I just said, "You know what?

00:01:13.147 --> 00:01:16.147
"Let's just try and make something upbeat

00:01:16.147 --> 00:01:18.847
"That could also be
played on acoustic guitar

00:01:18.847 --> 00:01:19.860
"Live basically."

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.420
And yeah, it just kind
of happened by accident.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.910
I wasn't expecting it to be first single.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.160
And yeah, it's one of these songs that...

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.650
It sort of came out, and
it's just kind of stuck.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.120
And it's not like...

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.560
It hasn't been like my
biggest charting single,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.670
but I think it'll end up

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.050
being one of my biggest
- [Kelly] Longevity.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:37.883
songs just over time

00:01:37.883 --> 00:01:39.870
very, very gradually.
- Yeah, that's longevity.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.130
- That's the best kind of song though.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.690
And also I didn't wanna freak you out,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:43.830
but my idea was actually

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.540
to completely do it with just a piano,

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.610
and I wanted to make
it really dark and sad,

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.080
and then I didn't wanna freak you out.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.970
So I kept it like this,

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.350
but I love a song like that.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.610
I feel like you write songs like that.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.230
That you can literally
do it with a huge band,

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:56.250
electric guitars, do it big.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.090
You could do dance.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.110
You could do singer songwriter.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.720
I think it's an amazing
gift you have, songwriting.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.430
Everybody knows that, but...

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:05.610
So you were a mega mentor
on The Voice this season.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:06.600
Super stoked about that.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.783
But I have to ask, who is
your favorite coach, Ed?

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.480
I mean, who is it?

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.320
Just shout it out.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.153
Just don't

00:02:14.153 --> 00:02:14.986
feel shy.
- Well, Kelly, only

00:02:14.986 --> 00:02:15.819
one person...

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:17.776
Only one person gave me a gift.

00:02:17.776 --> 00:02:19.634
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:20.467
- You're like,

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:21.780
"I can't say."
- [Ed] It must have been you

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.040
because I still actually...

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.990
I still have the jacket.

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.029
- See, I gave you

00:02:26.029 --> 00:02:26.862
presents.
- I still have the jacket

00:02:26.862 --> 00:02:28.387
in this house.

00:02:28.387 --> 00:02:31.020
- I will buy your love, Ed Sheeran.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.043
I will do it.

